00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:48.180
When the short put premium is collected at scale, the institution effectively sets a floor that can absorb selling pressure on down days.

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:57.100
Retail traders who skip this cross-check often enter names that look strong on flow alone, only to watch sector rotation pull the price lower anyway.

00:09:57.720 --> 00:10:06.260
Checking the 20-day average volume on the underlying equity alongside the options print adds one more layer that filters out noise from headline-driven spikes.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:17.060
Over time, this habit turns scattered options data into a repeatable filter that aligns individual sizing decisions, with the actual capital already committed by larger players.

